## Re-check collab modules after a stale DAB sync snapshot
================================================================================

Context:
The 0.9.0 app crashed on start with ``ModuleNotFoundError: No module named
'back.objects.registry.collab.EditLockService'``. The file is git-tracked and
not gitignored. The workspace ``collab/`` folder had CommentService,
ReviewService, and ``__init__.py``, but not EditLockService. The local DAB
sync snapshot still listed that path with the September mtime, so incremental
``bundle deploy`` skipped the upload. Step 6b only probed run.py / pyproject,
so auto-heal never fired.

Changes:

1. scripts/deploy.sh
   Add the collab package modules and ``digitaltwin/build/__init__.py`` to
   ``_CRITICAL_SYNCED_FILES`` so a missing boot module wipes the snapshot
   and re-syncs.
2. tests/units/api/test_help_api.py
   Guard that those paths stay in the step-6b list.

