## Mirror domain configuration to a per-instance GitHub repository
================================================================================

Context:
Admins want every domain's configuration (OWL, R2RML, layouts, rules, options)
versioned in a GitHub repository, one repository per OntoBricks instance.
Lakebase stays the source of truth. Each registry write queues an async,
coalesced push to GitHub. A manual "Load from GitHub repository" action in the
Registry import modal restores domains through the existing OBX preview/import
flow. Each version folder stores the split JSON sources plus generated OWL
(Turtle), R2RML (Turtle) and SHACL files. A GitHub failure never fails a
registry write.

Repository layout:
README.md, .ontobricks/{instance.json,global_config.json},
domains/<Folder>/domain.json,
domains/<Folder>/versions/V<n>/{manifest.json, info.json, ontology/*.json,
ontology/<Folder>.owl.ttl, ontology/<Folder>.shacl.ttl, mapping/assignment.json,
mapping/<Folder>.r2rml.ttl, layout/design.json, layout/views/*.json,
layout/map.json, metadata/tables.json}.
PUBLISHED versions are tagged ``<Folder>/V<n>``.

Changes:

1. src/back/core/github/{__init__.py,constants.py,GitHubClient.py}
   New GitHub Git Data API client (httpx): atomic multi-file commits with
   prefix replacement and deletes, fast-forward retry on 422, empty-repository
   bootstrap, tree listing, blob reads, lightweight tags. Errors are mapped to
   InfrastructureError / NotFoundError.
2. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubConfig.py
   Settings dataclass (owner, repo, branch, base_path, token secret scope/key,
   author, push_on_save, instance_uuid).
3. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/DomainRepoLayout.py
   Pure split/merge between a registry version document and the repository
   files. Produces stable sorted JSON and a manifest with sha256 hashes (no
   wall clock, so unchanged versions produce no commit). Scrubs secrets from
   info. Generates OWL/R2RML/SHACL Turtle, reporting failures instead of
   raising. Refuses manifests with a newer format_version.
4. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubSyncService.py
   push_version / delete_version / delete_domain / sync_all /
   build_obx_envelope against the RegistryStore interface. Instance claim via
   .ontobricks/instance.json (ConflictError unless take_over). Connection
   test checks push permission. Token comes from a Databricks secret
   (ONTOBRICKS_GITHUB_TOKEN env var as local fallback).
5. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubMirror.py
   Process-wide daemon worker with a queue coalesced by (folder, version) and
   a 2 s debounce. Mirror config is cached for 60 s. The commit actor comes
   from the request identity ContextVar. Last status is kept in memory for
   the Settings UI.
6. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubMirrorHooks.py,
   src/back/objects/registry/store/lakebase/store.py
   Mixin placed first in LakebaseRegistryStore's MRO. It notifies the mirror
   after a successful write_version, update_version_status, delete_version
   and delete_domain. Hooking at store level covers every write path and
   keeps RegistryService / Domain / SettingsService within their size
   budgets.
7. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/__init__.py
   Package re-exports.
8. src/back/objects/session/GlobalConfigService.py
   github_config key, get_github_config / set_github_config (setter
   normalises and invalidates the mirror config cache).
9. src/back/objects/domain/settings/GitHubSettings.py,
   src/back/objects/domain/settings/__init__.py
   Get/save (validation, instance_uuid generation), test, sync-all and the
   GitHub OBX envelope. Re-exported from the settings package.
10. src/api/routers/internal/settings.py
    Admin-only routes: GET/POST /settings/github, POST /settings/github/test,
    POST /settings/github/sync-all, GET /settings/github/obx.
11. src/front/config/menu_config.json,
    src/front/templates/settings.html,
    src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_github.html,
    src/front/static/config/js/settings-github.js
    New admin "GitHub" settings section: repository, branch, base path,
    secret scope/key picker, author, push-on-save, save/test/sync-all and the
    mirror status.
12. src/front/templates/partials/registry/_import_obx_modal.html,
    src/front/static/registry/js/registry.js
    "Load from GitHub repository" button that feeds the GitHub OBX envelope
    into the existing import preview/confirm flow.
13. tests/fixtures/github.py, tests/units/registry/test_github_layout.py,
    tests/units/registry/test_github_client.py,
    tests/units/registry/test_github_sync.py,
    tests/units/settings/test_github_settings.py
    In-memory GitHub fake (httpx.MockTransport) and tests for layout round
    trip, Turtle validity, client commits/retries/tags, sync, claim, mirror
    coalescing/status, store hooks and settings validation.
14. tests/units/front/test_sidebar_content_stretch_contract.py
    Add the github section to the settings inventory.
15. docs/user-guide.md, README.md, docs/sphinx/api/app.core.rst,
    docs/sphinx/api/app.core.github.rst,
    docs/sphinx/api/app.objects.registry.rst
    User guide section (setup, claim, push behaviour, layout, restore),
    README mention, and Sphinx API pages.

