## Log GitHub mirror pushes in the domain Audit trail
================================================================================

Context:
GitHub push outcomes were only visible as an in-memory "Last sync" line in
Settings → GitHub, lost on restart and not tied to a domain. They are now
persisted per domain version and shown on a new GitHub tab of Domain → Audit
trail. They reuse the existing domain_change_events log (source='github'), so
there is no new table or migration. Review-state logic is untouched.

Changes:

1. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubMirror.py
   New best-effort audit() that writes one change event (actions
   github_pushed, github_synced, github_version_deleted, github_push_failed)
   with meta: repository, commit_sha, commit_url, tag, message, errors.
   process() audits pushes that committed something or reported warnings,
   plus failures. Unchanged pushes and domain deletions (the domain row is
   gone) are not audited.
2. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubSyncService.py
   sync_all() also returns "pushed" (folder, version, per-version
   generation errors).
3. src/back/objects/registry/gitsync/GitHubConfig.py
   commit_url(sha) helper.
4. src/back/objects/domain/settings/GitHubSettings.py
   Sync all writes one github_synced audit row per mirrored version.
5. src/front/templates/partials/domain/_domain_audit.html,
   src/front/static/domain/js/domain-audit.js,
   src/front/static/domain/css/domain-audit.css
   New GitHub tab (commit link, tag, warnings or error, actor, repository).
   GitHub rows are excluded from the Ontology/Mapping tabs. New
   audit-marker-github style.
6. src/front/templates/partials/settings/_settings_github.html
   Pointer to Domain → Audit trail → GitHub under "Last sync".
7. tests/units/registry/test_github_sync.py
   Audit tests: push with commit link and tag, no-op not audited, failure
   audited, audit errors never raise, sync_all per-version report.
8. docs/user-guide.md
   "History in the Audit trail" paragraph in the GitHub section.

